Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||11-05-2001||03:47 PM||||the bralle buttons on the drive up atms can be explained very simply - all the ATMs are the same, the ones inthe stores, the malls, bank lobbies, and the drive throughs.<P> I problem I have is, when you use an ATM it askes you several questions on the display:<BR> 1. pin number<BR> 2. type of transaction.<BR> 3. which account?<BR> 4. do you want another transaction.<P> and sometimes it says things like: This will cost you a buck, do you want to continue?<P> or "insufficent funds" or account temporarlliy not accessable.<P>  how in the world is a blind person going to use this machine if they cant see the display? never mind the drivethrough, anywhere?!<P> the one that gets me is the sign on the post office door: "NO DOGS ALLOWED -except seeing eyes dogs"<P>  RUFF RUFF RUFF! "whats that Rusty? No dogs allowed?! OH no!<P>  Ruff ruff rrrrrrruffff ruff! "Except seeing eyes dogs - Oh OK! Good boy Rusty!"||||reg||1
